{"kind":"propose","text":"The live-only compact indexes reduced the admitted long-name baseline from 23,217,862 to 315,866 logical bytes. The oracle matched its item, snapshot, fixed counts, rekey order and rollback. I propose a 32 MiB hard logical ceiling under shipped bounds. A conservative initial estimate is 16,444,352 bytes, including one non-timed genesis item, typed self expansion, defaults, fixed rows and their unshared edges, binding names and state buckets, histories, duty and creation bookkeeping. The generation limit would fix min(32 MiB, charged creation plus fresh allowance). The allowance starts at four entry widths and adds capped declared item maxima times one entry width and their maximum timer reserve, using saturating arithmetic. A fresh turn still pays its actual charge before publication. I am filing the arithmetic and checking it against the compact representation. May I activate that policy after the bounds and native witnesses pass? The ceiling measures logical records, not host heap or concurrent-generation residency.","body":{"to":"planner"}}